    "description": "Random-init basin study, start 9 of 12. All eight gains initialised uniformly at random over their declared ranges; the body and world are held identical (body seed 1234, fixed terrain) and only the initial vector and the SEARCH rng differ, so any convergence is the criterion's doing. Run on both the CAD body and the measured body to ask whether the search finds a DIFFERENT operating point for a different machine.",
